Background

The Management of INDONGOZI SACCO NYAMASHEKE invites applications from qualified and interested candidates for the following vacant positions, as part of its efforts to strengthen its operations and improve service delivery.

Responsibilities

Duties include cash transactions, deposits and withdrawals, transfers, till management, daily balancing, loan disbursement, supporting documents, customer service and safeguarding funds.

Qualifications and Requirements

At least A2 in Accounting, or CMP certificate for completing Level One, or possessing the higher degree in Accounting, Finance, and management or any related field. Must have completed secondary education with 70% minimum marks.

Experience

Relevant experience in banking, SACCO, microfinance, cash handling or frontline financial services is an added advantage.

Other Employment Details

Full-time; Permanent subject to successful probation. Reporting to the Branch Operations Officer / Outlet Responsible.

Required Skills and Competencies

Good numerical and mathematical skills;

Accuracy and attention to detail;

Ability to handle cash and transactions responsibly;

Basic computer literacy, including CBS and Microsoft Office;

Good customer service skills;

Integrity, confidentiality and accountability;

Ability to work under pressure and meet deadlines.

General Requirements

Applicants must:

Meet the minimum academic and professional requirements for the position applied for;

Have the required experience, where applicable;

Demonstrate integrity, professionalism and good conduct;

Possess good communication, teamwork and interpersonal skills;

Have basic computer literacy relevant to the position;

Be willing to work at any branch or outlet of INDONGOZI SACCO NYAMASHEKE, as assigned by Management;

Be available to undergo the institution's recruitment and selection process.

